    "MOF use in wastewater treatment is limited by low stability in aqueous media, motivating conversion to carbon-containing derivatives.",
    "XRD and XPS showed adsorbed phosphorus formed zinc hydrogen phosphate on Zn-MOF but zinc phosphate on Zn-MOF-500.",
    "Zn-MOF-500 outperformed cited phosphate adsorbents including ZIF-8@MWCNT120 (203.0 mg/g), UiO-66-NH2 (92 mg/g), and Sn(II)-MOF (126.58 mg/g)."
